Id: stor018i
Severity: INFO
Category: filesystem
Check: check_storage
Fix: Add nodev,nosuid to /boot's fstab line; noexec to /dev through a drop-in for dev.mount.
References: mount(8); fstab(5); systemd mount-setup (src/core/mount-setup.c)
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST CM-6; ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

A hardening step past what any stock install does: a separate /boot is
mounted without nodev or nosuid, or /dev is mounted without noexec.
Both cost nothing and both change little. Only root writes to /boot,
so a setuid program or a device node there means root has already
been had; the kernel and initramfs are read by the boot loader before
Linux runs, so noexec on /boot would not change anything, and it is
not judged. systemd mounts /dev nosuid but not noexec, and the CIS
Benchmarks ask for neither; Lynis's checklist is stricter than
upstream here, so this stays informational.

To add them, put nodev,nosuid on /boot's line in /etc/fstab and
'mount -o remount /boot'; for /dev, a drop-in for dev.mount
('systemctl edit dev.mount', Options=nosuid,noexec,...) or a remount
in a boot-time unit.
